# .trivyignore
#
# CVEs that have been reviewed and accepted as unfixable or false-positive
# for the AchaeanFleet container images.
#
# Format: each entry MUST be preceded by a 6-field structured comment block
# per SECURITY.md "CVE Suppression Policy" / "Required entry format":
#
#   # <CVE-ID>
#   # Category: OS | npm | python | other
#   # Rationale: <why it cannot be fixed here>
#   # Exploitability: <none | low | medium | ...> — justification
#   # Expires: YYYY-MM-DD  (max 90 days from approval; re-review before)
#   # Reviewer: @<github-handle>  PR #<number>
#   <CVE-ID>
#
# Reference: https://aquasecurity.github.io/trivy/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/#trivyignore

# NOTE (issue #760, 2026-08-23): the 6 claude-code bundled-npm entries
# (CVE-2024-21538, CVE-2025-64756, CVE-2026-26996, CVE-2026-27903, CVE-2026-27904,
# CVE-2026-23745) and the 14 stale-published-image aider python entries
# (litellm trio incl. GHSA-69x8-hrgq-fjj8, aiohttp CVE-2025-69223, pillow trio,
# protobuf duo, pyasn1 duo, urllib3 trio) were pruned after fresh local Trivy
# scans of rebuilt achaean-claude and achaean-aider images confirmed they no
# longer fire (claude-code 2.1.233 bump + aider-chat 0.86.2 with
# vessels/aider/requirements-security-overrides.txt). See PR history for the
# removed structured blocks. Reproducible check: run
# scripts/verify-trivyignore-prune.sh (rebuilds + scans without --ignorefile);
# the CI "Trivy scan vessel image (gate)" jobs are the authoritative gate.

# NOTE (2026-11-06): the npm-bundled dependency entries CVE-2026-14257 and
# CVE-2026-69152 (brace-expansion) and CVE-2026-69192 (ip-address) were removed
# after expiring on 2026-11-05, and CVE-2026-73566 (tar) with them. Their
# rationale cited the npm 11.18.0 pin, which no longer exists: the base images
# and node-based vessels re-pin npm 11.19.1. Inspected in the published registry
# tarball (npm-11.19.1.tgz), that build bundles brace-expansion 5.0.9 (fix
# 5.0.8), ip-address 10.5.0 (fix 10.3.1) and tar 7.5.22 (fix 7.5.21), so the
# findings are resolved in the image rather than suppressed. The "Trivy scan
# vessel image (gate)" jobs are the authoritative check; if a finding reappears
# it comes from a package tree a vessel installs, and the replacement entry must
# name that package instead of npm.

# NOTE (2026-11-06): GHSA-f88m-g3jw-g9cj (sharp), GHSA-rgj7-g3m4-5g8c and
# GHSA-wq5f-xc86-pv6w were removed rather than renewed. The cline vessel moved
# from cline 2.14.0 to 2.18.0 and pins sharp through an npm `overrides` block in
# vessels/cline/Dockerfile. Local Trivy 0.76.2 scans (HIGH,CRITICAL,
# --ignore-unfixed) of node:26-slim images carrying cline 2.14.0 and cline
# 2.18.0 both report sharp 0.34.5 plus those three findings; the same image
# installed from /opt/cline/package.json with "overrides": {"sharp": "0.35.5"}
# reports no sharp findings, and its sharp round-trip (create -> png ->
# metadata) succeeds. The cline 3.x line also drops sharp, but it reintroduces
# fixable simple-git / @simple-git/argv-parser / @fastify/busboy / undici 5.x
# findings — see the CVE-2026-59723 entry for the scan diff.

# NOTE (2026-11-09, November re-review): 33 entries that expired on
# 2026-11-16 and two that expire on 2026-11-21 were re-checked against fresh
# scans instead of being renewed. The 2026-11-16 npm/python block was removed
# because none of it fires any more: a Trivy 0.76 HIGH,CRITICAL
# --ignore-unfixed scan of the achaean-claude image built in CI on 2026-11-09
# (run 42641850470, job 129246431256) reports the npm bundled tree at zero, and
# hand scans of achaean-aider:local and achaean-cline:local (same settings, no
# --ignorefile) report only pip-vendored setuptools CVE-2025-47273 (kept below)
# and cline's own CVE-2026-59723 (its own entry). The block's rationale had also
# drifted: it described npm 11.18.0 while the bases pin npm 11.21.2, and several
# entries labelled python findings (Pygments, aiohttp, python-dotenv, pip wheel)
# as "bundled npm CLI deps", which could never have been a correct chain.
# CVE-2026-56864/56865 went with them: they needed golang.org/x/mod 0.40.0, and
# the image's gh 2.103.3 pins x/mod v0.41.0. Re-add an entry only with a package
# and version that reproduces the finding.

# CVE-2026-39822
# Category: other
# Rationale: Go stdlib os.Root symlink-following, fixed in Go 1.26.5. Two vendored binaries in achaean-claude are still affected. (1) gitleaks v8.30.1 — the latest published release, pinned in ci/Containerfile — is built with Go 1.24.11; re-verified 2026-10-13 with Trivy 0.74.0 (`trivy rootfs` on the release tarball) and no newer release exists. (2) gh was installed unpinned from GitHub's apt repo; latest gh v2.102.0 (2026-09-30) is built with Go 1.27.1 and carries the fix, so the gh copy should clear on the next achaean-claude rebuild. PR #807 does not rebuild achaean-claude (Build Vessel Images is skipped), so the finding could not be re-scanned here and the entry is renewed rather than removed. yq was repaired independently by the v4.53.6 upgrade and no longer relies on this suppression. Tracking the remaining repair in #720/#779.
# Exploitability: low — os.Root traversal requires an attacker able to pre-place symlinks in directories gh opens via os.Root; gh runs as a developer CLI with no attacker-controlled filesystem input path in this vessel runtime. The gitleaks binary is a CI secret scanner with no untrusted filesystem input.
# Expires: 2027-01-11
# Reviewer: @mvillmow  PR #807 (re-review)
CVE-2026-39822

# CVE-2026-33818, CVE-2026-39821, CVE-2026-46600, CVE-2026-56853,
# CVE-2026-56858, CVE-2026-56859, CVE-2026-56860, CVE-2026-56862
# Category: other
# Rationale: golang.org/x/net cluster and golang stdlib compiled into the gitleaks binary (v8.30.1, pinned in ci/Containerfile). Fixed in Go 1.26.6 / 1.25.13 toolchains; no released gitleaks build vendors a newer stdlib. Re-verified 2026-10-13 with Trivy 0.74.0 against the v8.30.1 release tarball (`trivy rootfs`): every listed CVE still fires and v8.30.1 (2026-03-21) is still the latest published release. Correcting the original rationale: gitleaks is installed only into the achaeanfleet-ci container, which no Trivy image or filesystem scan covers, so these entries are defensive rather than load-bearing; they still hold if gitleaks is ever baked into a vessel image. This entry previously used a single non-conforming `# Expires:` line, so the expiry check in ci.yml never matched it; it is now in the required six-field form and is actively enforced. Same binary as CVE-2026-39822.
# Exploitability: low — gitleaks scans repository checkouts for secret patterns; no untrusted network input or attacker-supplied filesystem tree reaches it.
# Expires: 2027-01-11
# Reviewer: @mvillmow  PR #807 (re-review)
CVE-2026-33818
CVE-2026-39821
CVE-2026-46600
CVE-2026-56853
CVE-2026-56858
CVE-2026-56859
CVE-2026-56860
CVE-2026-56862

# CVE-2025-47273
# Category: python
# Rationale: setuptools 70.3.0 is vendored inside pip at pip/_vendor/setuptools.
# pip 26.3 is the pin in versions.yml and the newest published release, and it
# still vendors 70.3.0, so the copy cannot be replaced without forking pip; the
# site-packages setuptools is already 83.0.0. Verified 2026-11-09 with a Trivy
# HIGH,CRITICAL --ignore-unfixed scan of achaean-aider:local built from the
# pinned base, without --ignorefile: this is the only python finding in the
# venv. Tracking the pip re-vendor under issue #760.
# Exploitability: none — pip's vendored setuptools is internal to the installer
# and never reachable from vessel runtime code.
# Expires: 2027-02-07
# Reviewer: @mvillmow  PR #TBD (2026-11-09 re-review)
CVE-2025-47273

# CVE-2026-93687
# Category: npm
# Rationale: braces 3.0.3 is the latest published braces release and npm
# registry metadata reports no fixed version; Trivy lists the finding with an
# empty Fixed Version, so the `security-dependency-scan` gate fires it. Chain is
# markdownlint-cli2@0.23.2 (exact pin) -> micromatch@4.0.8 -> braces@^3.0.3.
# Clearing it needs either a braces 3.0.4 release or a markdownlint-cli2 release
# that drops the micromatch dependency; neither exists. Verified 2026-10-13
# against registry.npmjs.org.
# Exploitability: low — braces expands glob patterns. The only consumer is the
# Markdownlint toolchain in ci/, and its inputs are repository-controlled globs
# from .markdownlint.yaml; no attacker-supplied pattern reaches it.
# Expires: 2027-01-11
# Reviewer: @mvillmow  PR #807
CVE-2026-93687

# CVE-2026-102276, CVE-2026-102278
# Category: npm
# Rationale: brace-expansion 5.0.9 is bundled inside the npm CLI's own
# node_modules at /usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/brace-expansion
# in achaean-base-node, achaean-base-minimal and achaean-base-python. npm's
# bundled tree cannot be overridden without forking npm. Fix floors are 5.0.10
# (CVE-2026-102276) and 5.0.11 (CVE-2026-102278). Verified 2026-10-13 against
# the published npm tarballs: 11.19.1 (the pin in bases/Dockerfile.*),
# 12.0.0 and 12.2.0 (current latest) all bundle brace-expansion 5.0.9, so no
# released npm clears the floors. Same bundled-npm situation as CVE-2026-14257.
# Exploitability: none — brace-expansion is called with patterns that npm itself
# constructs internally; no attacker-controlled glob reaches the bundled copy in
# these base images.
# Expires: 2027-01-11
# Reviewer: @mvillmow  PR #807
CVE-2026-102276
CVE-2026-102278

# CVE-2026-19534
# Category: npm
# Rationale: undici 6.28.0 is bundled inside the npm CLI's own node_modules at
# /usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/undici in achaean-base-node,
# achaean-base-minimal and achaean-base-python. Fixed in 6.28.1. npm's bundled
# tree cannot be overridden without forking npm. Verified 2026-10-13 against the
# published npm tarballs: 11.19.1 (the pin), 12.0.0 and 12.2.0 all bundle
# undici 6.28.0.
# Exploitability: low — the advisory needs a remote server to negotiate an
# unrequested WebSocket subprotocol. npm is used only to install from pinned,
# checksum-verified public registries in these images; no attacker-controlled
# registry host is contacted.
# Expires: 2027-01-11
# Reviewer: @mvillmow  PR #807
CVE-2026-19534

# CVE-2026-97687, CVE-2026-97689
# Category: python
# Rationale: urllib3 2.7.0 is not a standalone install in achaean-base-python.
# It is vendored inside pip 26.2.1 at
# /usr/local/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pip/_vendor/urllib3, which the
# digest-pinned python:3.14-slim base provides. Fixed in 2.8.0. 26.2.1 is the
# newest published pip, so no pip release carries the fix yet, and a vendored
# dependency only moves when upstream pip re-vendors it. Confirmed 2026-10-13
# against pip's vendor.txt at tag 26.2.1 (`urllib3==2.7.0`) and the Trivy
# target table, which lists pip-26.2.1, msgpack and setuptools as the only
# python packages in the image.
# Exploitability: low — pip is a developer CLI in the image. CVE-2026-97687
# needs a TLS-intercepting HTTPS proxy the operator must configure, and
# CVE-2026-97689 needs an attacker-controlled endpoint for pip to download from.
# Expires: 2027-01-11
# Reviewer: @mvillmow  PR #807
CVE-2026-97687
CVE-2026-97689

# CVE-2026-103111, CVE-2026-86145, CVE-2026-89157, CVE-2026-89161
# Category: OS
# Rationale: libpcre2-8-0 10.42-1 is pulled in by git in achaean-athena-tools,
# which installs git from the pinned Debian snapshot. The fixes are Debian point
# releases (10.42-1+deb12u1 and 10.42-1+deb12u2) that have not been published
# for bookworm yet, so no snapshot can carry them. Verified 2026-10-13 against
# the live archive: deb.debian.org/debian/dists/bookworm/main offers only
# 10.42-1, and debian-security bookworm-security carries no libpcre2-8-0 entry
# at all. Re-checked 2026-11-06: the tracker now lists 10.42-1+deb12u2 as
# published, and this image pins snapshot 20261105T000000Z, so the rebuilt image
# should resolve git's pcre2 dependency to the fixed upload. The entry is kept
# until a scan of that rebuild confirms it, and should be deleted rather than
# renewed if the gate no longer reports these four IDs.
# Exploitability: low — pcre2 is reached through git's regex handling on
# attacker-supplied repository content; the image runs git only against the
# pinned Athena revision fetch, not against untrusted repositories.
# Expires: 2027-01-11
# Reviewer: @mvillmow  PR #807
CVE-2026-103111
CVE-2026-86145
CVE-2026-89157
CVE-2026-89161

# CVE-2026-78667, CVE-2026-78669, CVE-2026-97031
# Category: other
# Rationale: Go stdlib and golang.org/x/net compiled into /usr/bin/gh in
# achaean-claude. vessels/claude/Dockerfile installs gh unpinned from GitHub's
# apt repository, so the image carries gh v2.102.0 (2026-09-30), the latest
# published release, built with Go 1.27.1 and x/net v0.58.0. The fixes need Go
# 1.27.2 (or 1.26.9) and x/net 0.60.0; no released gh build vendors them, and
# gh is distributed as a prebuilt binary we cannot rebuild. Same binary and
# tracking as CVE-2026-39822 / CVE-2026-56864 / CVE-2026-56865 above (issue
# #720/#779). Verified 2026-10-13 with Trivy 0.74.0 against the v2.102.0
# linux_amd64 release tarball (`trivy rootfs`), which reproduces exactly these
# four findings under the gate's own severity and ignore-unfixed settings.
# Exploitability: low — all four are denial of service. CVE-2026-78667 and
# CVE-2026-78669 need crafted HTTP Range headers or HTTP/2 SETTINGS, and
# CVE-2026-97031 needs multiple ECH outer extension references. gh is a
# developer CLI in this vessel talking to api.github.com; no attacker-selected
# endpoint, and request headers are generated by gh rather than supplied.
# Expires: 2027-01-11
# Reviewer: @mvillmow  PR #807
CVE-2026-78667
CVE-2026-78669
CVE-2026-97031

# CVE-2026-59723
# Category: npm
# Rationale: cline 2.18.0 is installed in achaean-cline (bumped from 2.14.0);
# the fix needs cline 3.0.30 or newer, which is a major-version bump. cline
# 3.0.74 (latest, 2026-10-26) was scanned on 2026-11-06 with Trivy 0.76.2
# (HIGH,CRITICAL, --ignore-unfixed) and rejected: it drops sharp but pulls
# simple-git 3.36.0 (CVE-2026-102826/102827/102828, fixes 4.0.0/4.0.1),
# @simple-git/argv-parser 1.1.1 (CVE-2026-102829, fix 2.0.1),
# @fastify/busboy 2.1.1 (CVE-2026-19481, fix 3.2.1) and undici 5.29.0 via
# dify-ai-provider (CVE-2026-12151/1526/2229/109383/87018) — nine fixable
# HIGH/CRITICAL findings against this one. The advisory covers cross-origin
# WebSocket hijacking of the Cline Hub dashboard /browser endpoint. The Fleet
# vessel never runs that dashboard: vessels/cline/Dockerfile sets
# AGENT_PROGRAM=cline and the agent runs headless, the Dockerfile declares no
# EXPOSE, and compose/ maps no port for the vessel. Revisit when the 3.x line
# ships without those transitive regressions or a 2.x backport lands.
# Exploitability: none — no Cline Hub dashboard listener exists in this runtime,
# so the vulnerable endpoint is never bound.
# Expires: 2027-01-11
# Reviewer: @mvillmow  PR #823 (cline 2.18.0 bump)
CVE-2026-59723
